> Form a straight coupling and its target velocity

For data x=(2,0), base z=(0,0) and t=.25, the interpolated location is(.5,0), and the target velocity is x-z=(2,0). The fitted network learns this velocity from independent endpoint pairs; its learned ODE need not follow any individual straight training pair.

```{cpp, results="markdown", file="figures/flow_matching_worked.svg", flags="-std=c++23 -O2 $(pkg-config --cflags --libs datamunge) -Wl,-rpath,$(pkg-config --variable=libdir datamunge)"}
#include <dm/dm.hpp>
#include <iostream>
namespace n=dm::nn;namespace m=n::models;using T=n::Tensor;
int main(){std::filesystem::create_directories("build");
auto data=n::from_vector(std::vector<float>{2,0},{1,2}),noise=n::zeros({1,2});auto time=n::full({1,1},.25);T left=n::reshape(noise,{2}),right=n::reshape((1.-time)*noise+time*data,{2}),extra=n::reshape(data-noise,{2});
 auto av=left.to_vector<double>(),bv=right.to_vector<double>(),cv=extra.to_vector<double>();
 std::cout<<"| Base coordinate | Interpolated coordinate | Target velocity |\n|---:|---:|---:|\n";
 for(std::size_t i=0;i<av.size();++i)std::cout<<"|"<<av[i]<<"|"<<bv[i]<<"|"<<cv[i]<<"|\n";
 n::save_npz("build/flow_matching_worked.npz",{{"a",left},{"b",right},{"c",extra}});
 dm::graphics::RPlot::create().points(n::arange(0,std::int64_t(bv.size())).to_vector<double>(),bv,"Native worked values",{37,99,235},4).x_label("Coordinate / probe index").y_label("Native computed value").title("Form a straight coupling and its target velocity").size(900,500).save_svg("build/flow_matching_worked.svg");
}
